narrative:
Lady Marrow does not deny wanting the throne. Her daughter Corenna stands one step behind her, trying not to look like a weapon being held in reserve.

@Ysolde: The realm confuses inheritance with competence because inheritance is easier to recognize.
@Corenna: Mother.
@Ysolde: It is kinder that they hear it now.

The Hall of Claims fills with banners and lawyers. Herald Wexler Doone recites rules older than the kingdom's current borders. A dockworker in the gallery compares you to a dead hero from another age, then apologizes as if legacy were not already in the room.

@Wexler: By the twelfth binding of the river compact—
@Halvern: Please state the relevant part.
@Wexler: All of it is relevant.
